      "confidence": "derived",
      "derivation": "IS solved from the stated typical forward point, VF = 1.9 V at IF = 10 mA, with N = 2 and no series resistance: IS = IF / (e^(VF/(N·Vt)) − 1) = 8.7433e-19 A at Vt = 25.693 mV. One point fixes one unknown; N is the class’s.",
      "note": {
        "en": "Fitted at the sheet’s own test current, 10 mA, and nowhere else: the forward-current curve stops at 20 mA and is a figure, not a table. The fit reads 1.936 V at 20 mA, where a real part, with its few ohms of bulk resistance, reads a little higher.",
        "fr": "Ajusté au courant d’essai de la fiche, 10 mA, et nulle part ailleurs : la courbe du courant direct s’arrête à 20 mA, et c’est une figure, pas un tableau. L’ajustement lit 1.936 V à 20 mA, là où un vrai composant, avec ses quelques ohms de résistance de volume, lit un peu plus."
      }
    },
    "n": {
      "value": 2.0,
      "dimensionless": true,
